    content: "If you're considering dental implants in Palghar, the first question is almost always: how much will it cost? At Dental Solutions Palghar — a dedicated implant centre — we believe in complete pricing transparency, so here's the full 2026 price guide. A single-tooth dental implant in Palghar typically costs between ₹25,000 and ₹55,000 depending on the implant brand. Korean systems such as Osstem and Dentium start from ₹25,000-₹30,000 and offer excellent value with proven long-term results. Mid-range options like MIS (Israel) and Adin range from ₹35,000 to ₹40,000. Premium European brands — Straumann (Switzerland) and Nobel Biocare (Sweden) — cost ₹45,000 to ₹55,000 per implant and come with the strongest clinical evidence and lifetime warranties. This price is always all-inclusive: implant fixture + abutment + zirconia or PFM crown + 3D CBCT scan + all surgical and prosthetic visits. Watch out for clinics that quote ₹15,000 'starting' prices — these almost always exclude the abutment, crown, scans and follow-ups, and the final bill ends up 2-3× higher. For multiple missing teeth, an implant-supported 3-unit bridge (2 implants + 3 crowns) starts at ₹85,000 and is far more cost-effective than placing 3 separate implants. Full-arch rehabilitation using the All-on-4 protocol — replacing all teeth in one jaw on just 4 implants — starts from ₹2,50,000 per arch with acrylic teeth and ₹4,00,000 with premium zirconia. The All-on-6 variant adds 2 extra implants for ₹50,000 more and is recommended for heavy chewers. Additional procedures may be needed when bone is insufficient: sinus lift surgery costs ₹25,000-₹40,000, ridge augmentation/bone grafting ₹15,000-₹35,000, and advanced zygomatic implants ₹1,50,000 per implant. We offer 0% EMI on packages above ₹50,000 across major credit cards and partners like Bajaj Finserv, making world-class implants affordable on monthly payments as low as ₹4,500. What determines your final cost? The implant brand you choose, whether bone grafting is needed, the type of final crown (zirconia is premium), the number of teeth being replaced, and whether you opt for immediate-loading 'teeth in a day' protocols. The cheapest option is rarely the best — failed implants cost 3-4× more to replace, so prioritise the surgeon's experience, brand quality, and written warranty. At Dental Solutions Palghar we offer free implant consultations including a CBCT scan, so book a visit and get a written, all-inclusive quote with no obligation. Patients travel to us from across Palghar, Boisar, Tarapur, Virar, Vasai and Mumbai for our expertise, transparency and 4.9★ Google reviews.",
