    id: "20",
    title: "How to Choose the Best Dentist in Palghar: A 7-Point Checklist",
    excerpt: "Not all dental clinics in Palghar are equal. Use this 7-point checklist to pick a dentist who delivers safe, painless, high-quality care without overcharging.",
    content: "Picking the right dentist in Palghar matters far more than picking the right restaurant or hairdresser — a bad dental experience can cost you thousands of rupees and even your teeth. Here's the 7-point checklist we recommend every patient use before booking a long appointment with any dental clinic in Palghar. 1. Verify qualifications and registration. Every practising dentist in India must be registered with the State Dental Council (Maharashtra State Dental Council for Palghar) and hold a BDS or MDS degree. Look for the registration number displayed at the clinic and on the dentist's profile. Specialists (endodontists, orthodontists, periodontists, implantologists) should have an MDS in that specific field — not just a 'certificate' or short course. 2. Check Google reviews — but read them properly. A clinic with 200+ reviews averaging 4.7-4.9 stars and recent reviews mentioning specific treatments and dentist names is far more trustworthy than one with 20 generic 5-star reviews from the same week. Read the 3-star and 4-star reviews — they tell you the real strengths and weaknesses. 3. Ask about sterilisation protocols. A modern dental clinic uses Class B autoclaves (134°C steam sterilisation), single-use needles and burs, disposable instrument covers, and individually-packed sterile instrument trays opened in front of you. If a clinic can't explain its sterilisation protocol, walk out. 4. Demand transparent, written quotes. Avoid clinics that quote prices verbally or change them after starting treatment. A trustworthy dentist in Palghar provides a written, itemised quote covering the procedure, materials (brand of implant/crown/aligner), number of visits, what's included, and what's not included. 5. Check the equipment. Quality dental care requires modern equipment: digital X-rays (lower radiation than film), an RVG sensor, ideally an in-house CBCT machine for implants, rotary endodontics for root canals, and an apex locator. Older clinics still using film X-rays and manual instruments deliver less predictable results. 6. Watch out for over-treatment. If a dentist recommends 8 fillings, 2 root canals and a crown in your first visit, get a second opinion. Honest dentists in Palghar prioritise prevention, suggest conservative treatments first, and only recommend major work when truly needed. Red flags: pressure to start treatment immediately, refusal to share X-rays, no written diagnosis. 7. Visit the clinic before booking major treatment. A 15-minute consultation tells you everything: Is the clinic clean? Does the dentist listen and explain in your language? Are the staff respectful? Is the equipment modern? Are there before-and-after photos of real patients? Does the dentist show you your X-rays and explain your case? At Dental Solutions Palghar we welcome second opinions and offer free initial consultations — we believe an informed patient is a happy long-term patient. Whether you choose us or another clinic, use this checklist and you'll find a dentist in Palghar you can trust for life.",
