    id: "23",
    title: "Painless Root Canal Treatment in Palghar: Single-Sitting RCT Explained",
    excerpt: "Modern single-sitting root canal treatment in Palghar takes 45-90 minutes and is genuinely painless. Here's how our endodontist makes it possible.",
    content: "The phrase 'root canal' still makes people flinch, but root canal treatment in 2026 is nothing like the multi-visit ordeal your parents remember. At Dental Solutions Palghar, most root canals are completed in a single sitting of 45-90 minutes using rotary endodontic instruments, an apex locator and 3D-guided diagnosis. Here's what makes single-sitting RCT painless and predictable. We use a topical anaesthetic gel before the local anaesthetic injection, so the injection itself is barely felt. We use buffered lignocaine with adrenaline which acts faster and lasts longer than older formulations, ensuring complete numbness throughout the procedure. Once numb, the tooth is isolated with a rubber dam (no water in your mouth, no taste of medicaments), and rotary nickel-titanium files clean and shape the canals in a fraction of the time hand files take. An electronic apex locator measures canal length precisely, so we don't over-instrument or leave infection behind. The canals are then sealed with gutta-percha and a biocompatible sealer, and the tooth is built up with composite ready for a crown. Most patients walk out chewing soft food on the same side within 2 hours. Cost of root canal treatment in Palghar at our clinic ranges from ₹4,500 (anterior teeth) to ₹7,500 (molars with extra canals), with discounts when combined with a zirconia or PFM crown. Single-sitting RCT is suitable for 85% of cases — the exceptions are heavily infected teeth with abscesses, which need a 2-visit protocol with intracanal medication. If you've been told you need a root canal and you're dreading it, book a consultation — we'll show you exactly what's involved and most of our patients describe the experience as 'no different from a filling'.",
