    id: "25",
    title: "Wisdom Tooth Removal in Palghar: Cost, Recovery & When You Really Need It",
    excerpt: "Not every wisdom tooth needs to come out. Here's when extraction is genuinely necessary, what it costs in Palghar, and what recovery actually feels like.",
    content: "Wisdom teeth (third molars) erupt between ages 17 and 25 and they're the single most common reason adults visit an emergency dentist in Palghar. But contrary to common belief, not every wisdom tooth needs removal. Our oral surgeon's rule: extract only when the tooth is causing problems or has a high risk of causing them. Definite reasons to remove a wisdom tooth: recurrent pericoronitis (gum infection around a partially-erupted tooth), decay in the wisdom tooth or the second molar in front of it caused by food trapping, cyst formation visible on X-ray or CBCT, damage to the adjacent tooth's root, and persistent pain. Reasons that often don't need extraction: a fully-erupted, well-positioned wisdom tooth that you can clean properly; a deeply impacted wisdom tooth that's completely buried in bone, asymptomatic, and shows no pathology on imaging. Cost of wisdom tooth removal in Palghar at Dental Solutions Palghar: simple extraction (fully erupted) ₹1,500-₹2,500; surgical extraction (partially erupted or impacted) ₹4,500-₹8,500 depending on depth and complexity; all four wisdom teeth in one sitting under IV sedation ₹25,000-₹35,000. Every surgical wisdom tooth extraction at our clinic includes a pre-op CBCT scan to map the inferior alveolar nerve (the nerve that gives you feeling in your lower lip and chin) — this is non-negotiable for lower wisdom teeth and is what prevents the rare but serious complication of nerve injury. Recovery: most patients return to office work in 2 days, eat normal food in 5-7 days, and have full healing in 2-3 weeks. We prescribe antibiotics, anti-inflammatory pain relief, and a chlorhexidine mouthwash. Expect mild swelling for 48 hours (use ice packs), some bruising, and difficulty opening your mouth fully for a few days. If you're 18-30 and have never had your wisdom teeth assessed, book a panoramic X-ray review — many problems are easier to prevent before they start.",
