    excerpt: "Not all dental implants are equal. We compare the four most-used implant brands in Palghar by price, success rates, warranty and ideal use case.",
    content: "When you book a dental implant in Palghar, the single biggest cost variable is the implant brand. Branded implants from Nobel Biocare or Straumann cost 2-3x as much as Indian or Korean implants — so are they worth it? Here's the honest engineer's-eye comparison from Dental Solutions Palghar's implant centre. Nobel Biocare (Switzerland) is the original dental implant brand, with 50+ years of clinical data and 95-98% 10-year success rates. Price per implant in Palghar (with abutment and zirconia crown): ₹55,000-₹75,000. Lifetime implant warranty. Best for: front teeth, immediate-load cases, full-arch rehabilitation, patients who want the most-documented system. Straumann (Switzerland) is the global market leader with their SLA and SLActive surface technologies that integrate with bone faster than any other implant. Price: ₹55,000-₹80,000. Lifetime warranty. Best for: smokers, diabetics, immediate placement after extraction, and bone-grafted sites where faster integration matters. Osstem (Korea) is the largest Asian implant manufacturer and offers the best balance of quality and price. Price: ₹30,000-₹40,000 fully loaded. 10-year clinical data is strong with 94-96% success rates. Best for: most standard implant cases — single tooth replacements, multi-tooth bridges. This is what we recommend for the majority of our Palghar patients. Adin (Israel) and Dentium (Korea) offer reliable mid-range implants at ₹25,000-₹32,000. Good for budget cases with healthy bone. Indian implants (Equinox, Genesis, etc.) start at ₹18,000-₹22,000 fully loaded. They work, but clinical data is thinner and we use them only in carefully selected cases. Why brand matters: implant surfaces (the microscopic texture that bone grows into), thread design (how the implant grips bone), and abutment fit (the connection between implant and crown) are what determine long-term success. Cheap implants often have inferior surface treatments, looser abutment connections (which loosen over years), and limited prosthetic component availability if your crown ever needs replacement. At Dental Solutions Palghar we stock Nobel, Straumann, Osstem and Adin in-house, and we'll recommend the brand based on your specific case — not the most expensive one available.",
