    title: "Dental Insurance & EMI Options in Palghar: How to Pay for Major Dental Work",
    excerpt: "Implants, full-mouth rehab and braces are major investments. Here's how to use insurance, no-cost EMI and cashless options at dental clinics in Palghar.",
    content: "Major dental work — implants, full-mouth rehabilitation, orthodontics or smile makeovers — can run into lakhs of rupees, and most Indian health insurance policies don't cover routine dentistry. Here's how to make it affordable at Dental Solutions Palghar and most other reputable clinics in the area. 1. Health insurance — what it does cover. Most policies (Star Health, HDFC Ergo, Niva Bupa, ICICI Lombard, etc.) cover dental treatment only when it's required due to accidental injury or as part of a hospitalisation. So if you chip a tooth in a road accident or need oral surgery under general anaesthesia, you can usually claim. Always submit a pre-authorisation with X-rays and a detailed treatment plan. 2. Corporate group insurance and ESIC. Many corporate group policies include a dental sub-limit of ₹5,000-₹25,000 per year covering scaling, fillings and X-rays. ESIC covers most basic dental procedures at empanelled clinics for industrial workers in Tarapur and Boisar — check your eligibility card. 3. Dental-specific insurance. Standalone dental insurance is still rare in India but a few insurers (ManipalCigna ProHealth Plus, Care Health Joy) include enhanced dental cover. Read the fine print: most have a 1-2 year waiting period for major procedures. 4. No-cost EMI on credit cards. We offer 3, 6, 9 and 12-month no-cost EMI on HDFC, ICICI, Axis, SBI, Kotak and Yes Bank credit cards for treatment values above ₹10,000. This is the most-used option at our clinic — a ₹60,000 implant becomes ₹5,000/month for 12 months at zero interest. 5. Bajaj Finserv and ZestMoney. For patients without credit cards, Bajaj Finserv Health EMI Card and ZestMoney offer dental loans up to ₹4 lakh with EMI tenures of 3-24 months. Approval is usually within an hour with PAN, Aadhaar and a bank statement. 6. In-house instalment plans. For long orthodontic and implant cases, we offer a stage-wise payment plan with no interest — pay as treatment progresses, not upfront. 7. Discounts that genuinely exist. Combined treatments (e.g., scaling + 3 fillings, or implant + crown) come with package pricing that's 10-15% cheaper than itemised quotes. Senior citizens and serving defence personnel get 10% off most procedures at our clinic. Never let cost stop you from getting essential dental work — untreated decay and gum disease lead to far more expensive problems later. Book a free financial consultation alongside your clinical exam and we'll put a realistic, written plan together.",
